WEBVTT

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.640
Structured techniques are most valuable when used consistently.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.915
Analysts should remain curious, document assumptions, welcome feedback,

00:00:06.915 --> 00:00:11.260
communicate uncertainty honestly, and revise conclusions when evidence changes.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.880
Analytical discipline requires humility.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.725
A strong analyst can explain confidence levels, acknowledge gaps,

00:00:15.725 --> 00:00:18.175
and separate what is known from what is inferred.

00:00:18.175 --> 00:00:21.840
Over time, these habits improve both individual and team performance.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.145
They make analysis easier to review, challenge, brief, and update.

00:00:25.145 --> 00:00:26.380
The goal is not perfection.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.540
The goal is becoming more thoughtful, transparent,

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.020
and disciplined in how judgments are formed and communicated.
